Name the two pairs of parallel lines and two pairs of perpendicular lines shown by the marks. Write your answers using symbols.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (J) at (0,2.6);
\coordinate (K) at (3.8,2.6);
\coordinate (L) at (0,0);
\coordinate (M) at (3.8,0);
\draw (J)--(K)--(M)--(L)--cycle;
\draw (0.32,2.6)--(0.32,2.28)--(0,2.28);
\draw (3.48,2.6)--(3.48,2.28)--(3.8,2.28);
\draw (1.72,2.76)--(1.92,2.6)--(1.72,2.44);
\draw (1.72,0.16)--(1.92,0)--(1.72,-0.16);
\draw (-0.16,1.12)--(0,1.32)--(0.16,1.12);
\draw (-0.16,1.38)--(0,1.58)--(0.16,1.38);
\draw (3.64,1.12)--(3.8,1.32)--(3.96,1.12);
\draw (3.64,1.38)--(3.8,1.58)--(3.96,1.38);
\path (J) node[above left] {$J$};
\path (K) node[above right] {$K$};
\path (L) node[below left] {$L$};
\path (M) node[below right] {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name a set of three parallel lines. Which line is perpendicular to all three? Write the relationships using symbols.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.2,1.2)--(2.2,1.2);
\draw (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw (-2.2,-1.2)--(2.2,-1.2);
\draw (0,-1.8)--(0,1.8);
\draw (-1.6,-1.8)--(1.6,1.8);
\draw (-1.5,1.36)--(-1.3,1.2)--(-1.5,1.04);
\draw (-1.5,0.16)--(-1.3,0)--(-1.5,-0.16);
\draw (-1.5,-1.04)--(-1.3,-1.2)--(-1.5,-1.36);
\draw (0.25,1.2)--(0.25,1.45)--(0,1.45);
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\draw (0.25,-1.2)--(0.25,-0.95)--(0,-0.95);
\path (-2.2,1.2) node[left] {$J$};
\path (2.2,1.2) node[right] {$K$};
